\title{sbom: Create, Read and Validate Software Bills of Materials}
\description{
Create software bills of materials for 'R' packages, projects and 'Shiny' apps from installed libraries, package sources, 'renv' lockfiles, 'Posit Connect' manifests and 'Nix' environments written by 'rix', including the system libraries and bundled code that packages carry. Write them as 'CycloneDX' 1.4 to 1.7 documents, Software Package Data Exchange ('SPDX') 2.2, 2.3 and 3.0.1 documents or Software Identification ('SWID') tags, or as a comma-separated values (CSV) inventory, and read and combine bills of materials that any tool wrote. Check each document against the schema that its specification publishes, or structural rules where that schema is not bundled, against integrity rules, and against the minimum elements of the National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA). On request, list the security advisories that Open Source Vulnerabilities ('OSV') publishes for the exact package versions.
